{\small

\begin{itemize}

\item[S1] ULAM.AI, \emph{UnsolvedMath}, supplied \texttt{problems.json}, record 171 (GREEN-083), statement and background. The embedded literature-review date is 2026-08-17; that is the archive’s review date, not a fresh certification. Dataset landing page: \url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.

\item[S2] F. Manners, A solution to the pyjama problem, Invent. Math. 202 (2015), 239-270, \nolinkurl{doi:10.1007/s00222-014-0571-7.} \url{https://arxiv.org/abs/1305.1514}. Bibliographic information imported from the supplied record.

\item[S3] N. Kravitz, J. Leng, Quantitative pyjama, arXiv:2510.17744 (2025). \url{https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.17744}. Bibliographic information imported from the supplied record.

\item[S4] B. Green, 100 Open Problems, Problem 41, version. \url{https://people.maths.ox.ac.uk/greenbj/papers/open-problems.pdf}. The author-hosted document was inspected on 27 September 2026; the archive’s local code is not a problem-number locator in this paper.

\item[E1] N. Kravitz and J. Leng, \emph{Quantitative pyjama}, 2025. \url{https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.17744}. Inspected 1 October 2026.

\end{itemize}

}

